      "reasoning": "I'll hold priority here. Blocking Eloise with Serra Angel (4/4 vs 4/4) is a trade, but Eloise has a death trigger (\"Whenever another creature you control dies...\"). If Serra dies, she's not \"another creature you control\" for Sonnet, so Eloise triggers won't happen from Serra dying. Wait, Eloise says \"Whenever another creature *you control* dies\". If Eloise dies at the same time as Serra, and no other creature of Sonnet's dies, no trigger. However, if Sonnet has a trick, I might lose Serra.\n\
\n\
Wait, looking at the board:\n\
My `Serra Angel` (4/4) is blocking `Eloise, Nephalia Sleuth` (4/4).\n\
My `Voice of All` is on the battlefield, tapped (it came in attacking last turn with Kaalia).\n\
I have 5 mana available. Hand: `Mountain`, `Lightkeeper of Emeria`, `Mountain`, `Akoum Refuge`. Nothing with flash.\n\
\n\
I've already declared blockers (`Serra` blocking `Eloise`). Now I have priority in the Declare Blockers step.\n\
If I do nothing, damage happens. 4 damage to Serra, 4 damage to Eloise. Both die.\n\
Eloise is a 4/4. Serra is a 4/4.\n\
Sonnet (Eloise's controller) might have a trick, but they are tapped out mostly?\n\
Sonnet's lands: Island (tapped), Sunken Hollow (tapped), Swamp (Untapped), Island (tapped), Command Tower (tapped), Swamp (tapped).\n\
Only `p26` Swamp is untapped? No wait, `p26` Swamp is `tapped: false` in the `get_game_state`.\n\
Actually `p26` was tapped in previous logs?\n\
Let's look at `get_game_state` result `0t8hXzUcb2iP0b1GlazF`:\n\
Sonnet lands:\n\
`p13` Island (tapped)\n\
`p14` Sunken Hollow (tapped)\n\
`p26` Swamp (false - Untapped)\n\
`p34` Island (tapped)\n\
`p44` Command Tower (tapped)\n\
`p48` Swamp (tapped)\n\
Sonnet has 1 Black mana available.\n\
Sonnet also has `Hordewing Skaab` (3/3) which just entered (summoning sickness).\n\
\n\
If I trade Serra for their Commander Eloise, that's generally a fine trade for me. Eloise is an engine piece. Serra is just a beater/blocker. I have `Lightkeeper` in hand to rebuild.\n\
\n\
I have no instants. I will pass priority.\n\
\n\
One detail: `Voice of All` has Protection from Black. Eloise is Blue/Black. If I had blocked with Voice of All, it would have been a free block. But Voice of All is tapped (it entered tapped and attacking on my turn). So I couldn't block with it. Serra was my only untapper (Vigilance).\n\
\n\
So the block is locked in. Time to trade.\n\
\n\
One small note: \"Undead on wings? Looks like target practice to me.\" was sent.\n\
\n\
I'll pass priority.\n\
