But Kaalia? Kaalia is white/black/red.\n\
Maybe `Bathe in Light` was used?\n\
It's in my graveyard (`p72`).\n\
Wait, I used Bathe in Light turn 6/7?\n\
Ah, if Bathe in Light gave protection from White, it would save my creatures from Winds of Rath?\n\
No, \"Global\" effects like sweepers don't target, so Protection doesn't help unless it prevents damage.\n\
Winds says \"Destroy all creatures\". Protection prevents: Damaged, Enchanted/Equipped, Blocked, Targeted.\n\
It does NOT prevent \"Destroy\".\n\
So unless my creatures were indestructible or phased out...\n\
Wait, maybe Winds of Rath happened BEFORE I played Kaalia?\n\
No, Kaalia was turn 6.\n\
Maybe Winds of Rath failed? Or was countered?\n\
Or maybe it happened a long time ago and I just saw it now?\n\
No, it's `p81`.\n\
Maybe my creatures ARE dead and the game state is lagging?\n\
No, pass_priority says they are attackers.\n\
And I see them on battlefield.\n\
Okay, I assume they are alive.\n\
\n\
Gem3F: 40 life. `Galea` (7/7) + 5 Saprolings.\n\
Sonnet: 17 life. NO CREATURES.\n\
Qwen3: DEAD.\n\
\n\
So it's Me (29) vs Gem3F (40) vs Sonnet (17).\n\
\n\
Sonnet has no creatures.\n\
Gem3F has 5 Saprolings + Galea.\n\
Galea is tapped? No, `tapped:false`.\n\
Saprolings: 3 tapped, 2 summoning sick.\n\
So Gem3F has 1 blocker (Galea).\n\
Wait, \"Saproling Token... tapped:true\".\n\
Ah, 3 are tapped.\n\
2 are summoning sick (tapped:false).\n\
Can summoning sick creatures block? Yes.\n\
So Gem3F has: Galea (7/7), 2 Saprolings (1/1). Total 3 blockers.\n\
I have: Kaalia (2/2 flier), Voice (2/2 flier), Lightkeeper (2/4 flier).\n\
Does Galea have reach/flying?\n\
No. `Verdant Embrace` gives +3/+3 and Saprolings.\n\
Unless Galea has other improvements.\n\
Currently shows Power 7, Toughness 7.\n\
Base 4/4 + 3/3 = 7/7.\n\
No other equipment shown.\n\
Only `Verdant Embrace` attached (p77).\n\
So Galea DOES NOT have Reach/Flying.\n\
Saprolings are 1/1 green. No Reach.\n\
So my creatures are UNBLOCKABLE by Gem3F.\n\
\n\
I can hit Gem3F for 6 damage. Down to 34.\n\
Or hit Sonnet for 6. Down to 11.\n\
\n\
Gem3F is the threat with 40 life and token generation.\n\
Sonnet is drawing cards but has no board.\n\
I should focus Gem3F?\n\
But 40 life is a lot.\n\
Maybe I kill Sonnet first?\n\
Sonnet is at 17. 3 hits.\n\
Gem3F is at 40. 7 hits.\n\
If I leave Sonnet alone, they might dig for answers (board wipe).\n\
Sonnet is blue/black (Zombie deck).\n\
`Empty the Laboratory` in graveyard.\n\
If Sonnet wipes the board, I lose my army.\n\
Gem3F already used Winds of Rath (white wipe).\n\
Gem3F is Bant (G/W/U).\n\
So both have wipes.\n\
\n\
If I attack Sonnet, I put them in lethal range faster.\n\
If I attack Gem3F, I chip away but they gain life? No, Verdant Embrace doesn't gain life.\n\
But Galea is huge.\n\
If Gem3F attacks me, I take 7+.\n\
I have 29. I can take a hit.\n\
\n\
I will attack Sonnet.\n\
Get them to 11.\n\
Next turn 5.\n\
Then dead.\n\
\n\
Or maybe split?\n\
No, focus fire is better.\n\
Sonnet is open.\n\
Gem3F is open to fliers.\n\
I'll specific target Sonnet.\n\
\n\
Actually, Gem3F has `Galea`. If Galea has vigilance (does she?), she can attack and block.\n\
Galea text: \"Vigilance. You may look at top card... You may cast Auras/Equipment...\".\n\
Yes, Galea has Vigilance.\n\
So she can attack me for 7 and still block.\n\
But she can't block FLIERS.\n\
So I am safe to attack Gem3F.\n\
But Sonnet is weaker.\n\
\n\
I'll go for Sonnet.\n\
I want to eliminate players to reduce board wipes/removals.\n\
Qwen3 is gone.\n\
Sonnet is next.\n\
\n\
My hand: Lands.\n\
Play a land: `Swamp` (p88) or `Mountain` (p4).\n\
I have `Akoum Refuge` (played last turn).\n\
I'll play a Swamp.\n\
\n\
(Chat: \"Sonnet, you're looking a bit exposed there.\")\n\
\n\
Play Swamp. Attack Sonnet with all.\n\
\n\
