      "decision_index": 173,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Coach attacked Qwen3 Spike (at 21 life, no creatures) with only Lightkeeper of Emeria (2 damage) instead of all three flying creatures (Kaalia 2/2, Voice of All 2/2, Lightkeeper 2/4) for 6 total damage. Qwen3 has no blockers, so there's no combat risk. This leaves 4 free damage on the table.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Lightkeeper of Emeria for 2 flying damage",
      "better_line": "Attack with all three creatures (Kaalia, Voice of All, Lightkeeper) for 6 damage against an opponent with no blockers. Even though Kaalia's trigger has no targets in hand, the 2 extra damage from each additional attacker is free.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 190,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 184,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player's reasoning incorrectly assumes Galea is on the battlefield and would survive Winds of Rath. In reality, Gem3F Stoic's battlefield only has Sram and Puresteel Paladin, both of which die to the wipe. While the wipe does remove threats like Kaalia and Hordewing Skaab, it also destroys the player's own key equipment-synergy engines with no surviving creature to rebuild around. The player made this decision based on a fundamentally incorrect read of their own board state.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Winds of Rath, destroying all creatures including their own Sram and Puresteel Paladin, believing Galea would survive.",
      "better_line": "Hold Winds of Rath for a turn when you have a creature that would survive (e.g., one enchanted with Imprisoned in the Moon on an opponent's threat doesn't help here). Consider using Imprisoned in the Moon on Kaalia now to neutralize the biggest threat while keeping your engine creatures alive, then wipe later if needed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 208,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 198,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic declined to cast Imprisoned in the Moon on Kaalia of the Vast, one of the most dangerous commanders on the board. Kaalia cheats in Angels/Demons/Dragons on attack, and Imprisoned in the Moon is one of the best answers since it doesn't send the commander back to the command zone. While Kaalia is currently tapped, there's no strategic benefit to waiting - Stoic has no creatures to use Valorous Stance's indestructible mode on, and holding up mana accomplishes little.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting either spell in hand.",
      "better_line": "Cast Imprisoned in the Moon targeting Kaalia of the Vast to permanently neutralize the most threatening commander on the board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 239,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 223,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic sent all attackers including Galea (7/7 vigilance) at Qwen3 Spike who is at 2 life. Three 1/1 Saprolings alone are sufficient for lethal since Qwen3 has only one blocker (Dawnhart Wardens 3/3) and all lands tapped (no tricks). Galea's 7 damage is wasted overkill when it could pressure another opponent, especially since Galea has vigilance and would remain untapped for defense.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with all creatures (Galea + 3 Saprolings) at Qwen3 Spike",
      "better_line": "Attack with only the 3 Saprolings at Qwen3 Spike (guaranteed lethal through one blocker with all Qwen3 lands tapped) and send Galea at Sonnet Vorthos or Gem3P Coach for 7 free damage while keeping Galea untapped as a blocker via vigilance.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 240,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 233,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic is missing lethal on Qwen3 Spike (at 2 life). By splitting attacks - sending only two 1/1 Saprolings at Qwen3 and Galea at Sonnet - Dawnhart Wardens (3/3) blocks one Saproling, and only 1 damage gets through, leaving Qwen3 at 1 life. Sending all three attackers (Galea + both Saprolings) at Qwen3 would be lethal: Wardens can only block one creature, and the remaining attackers deal at least 2 damage (enough to kill from 2 life). Galea has vigilance so it stays untapped for defense regardless.",
      "action_taken": "Split attacks: two Saprolings at Qwen3 Spike (2 life) and Galea at Sonnet Vorthos (24 life), dealing only 1 damage to Qwen3 after a block",
      "better_line": "Attack with all three creatures (Galea + both Saprolings) at Qwen3 Spike. Dawnhart Wardens blocks one attacker, remaining attackers deal at least 2 damage for lethal. Galea's vigilance means no defensive cost.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 240,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 233,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Qwen3 Spike is at 2 life with only Dawnhart Wardens (3/3) as a potential blocker. Galea (4/4 vigilance) attacking Qwen3 Spike is lethal - either they don't block and die, or they block and lose their only creature while Galea survives. Instead, Gem3F Stoic attacked Sonnet Vorthos at 24 life for an inconsequential 4 damage.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked Sonnet Vorthos (24 life) with Galea for 4 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack Qwen3 Spike (2 life) with Galea for a guaranteed kill, eliminating a player from the game.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 240,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 233,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic missed lethal on Qwen3 Spike who is at 2 life. They had Imprisoned in the Moon in hand (cost {2}{U}) with plenty of mana available. They could have cast Imprisoned in the Moon on Dawnhart Wardens (Qwen3 Spike's only blocker) during their first main phase, then attacked Qwen3 Spike with Galea (4/4) for lethal damage. Instead, they chose to attack Sonnet Vorthos at 24 life.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked Sonnet Vorthos (at 24 life) instead of Qwen3 Spike (at 2 life)",
      "better_line": "Cast Imprisoned in the Moon on Dawnhart Wardens in first main phase to remove the only blocker, then attack Qwen3 Spike with Galea for lethal (4 damage vs 2 life)",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 240,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 233,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Kaalia of the Vast is the most dangerous threat on the board, capable of cheating massive creatures into play every attack. Gem3F Stoic had Imprisoned in the Moon in hand with plenty of mana to cast it, and Kaalia was tapped with Coach's mana mostly tapped (reducing risk of interaction). Letting Kaalia survive to attack again next turn risks another free creature drop.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells, leaving 8 mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast Imprisoned in the Moon targeting Kaalia of the Vast, neutralizing Coach's commander by turning it into a colorless land. This removes the primary threat engine on the board at minimal risk.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 246,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 236,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player references targeting Liliana's Devotee with Imprisoned in the Moon, but Liliana's Devotee is not on any battlefield. The most impactful target available is Kaalia of the Vast, which is the biggest threat on the board - it cheats in powerful creatures on attack and has Anger in Coach's graveyard giving it haste with a Mountain. Targeting anything other than Kaalia wastes a premium removal spell.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Imprisoned in the Moon intending to target Liliana's Devotee (which doesn't exist on the battlefield)",
      "better_line": "Cast Imprisoned in the Moon targeting Kaalia of the Vast, the most dangerous threat on the board that generates massive value each attack step",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 261,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 251,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Kaalia of the Vast is the most dangerous creature on the board - she cheats Angels, Demons, and Dragons into play for free when attacking, and Coach has Anger in the graveyard potentially granting haste. Imprisoning Kaalia would neutralize Coach's primary engine. Instead, the player targeted Liliana's Devotee, a relatively minor 2/3 creature that gives Zombies +1/+0 when Sonnet has no other Zombies on board.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Liliana's Devotee with Imprisoned in the Moon instead of the much more threatening Kaalia of the Vast.",
