      "decision_index": 253,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic has lethal on board against Sonnet Vorthos (11 life) with Galea (7 power) + 6 Saprolings (6 damage) = 13 damage, but only selected a single Saproling as an attacker instead of attacking with all creatures for the kill.",
      "action_taken": "Selected only one Saproling (p86) as an attacker",
      "better_line": "Attack with all creatures (Galea + 6 Saprolings) directed at Sonnet Vorthos for 13 damage, which is lethal against their 11 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 264,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 260,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic declined to use Bant Charm to remove Kaalia of the Vast during combat while it was tapped. Kaalia is an extremely dangerous value engine that generates free creatures on every attack. With no creatures on board and facing a 1v1 against Coach, removing the key threat was important. Stoic had the mana available (Forest, Island, Command Tower/Exotic Orchard for W).",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells during combat.",
      "better_line": "Cast Bant Charm targeting Kaalia of the Vast, putting it on the bottom of Coach's library, permanently removing the most dangerous threat and preventing future value generation from attacks.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 277,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 274,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3P Coach declined to attack with Voice of All when Gem3F Stoic had zero creatures on the battlefield. The reasoning about blocking Galea and Saprolings appears to reference creatures that aren't actually on the board. With no blockers and no creatures to crack back, attacking for 2 was free damage in a game where Coach is behind 14 to 34 life.",
      "action_taken": "Did not attack with Voice of All, keeping it back to block nonexistent threats.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Voice of All for 2 free damage against an empty board, reducing the life differential in a game where Coach needs to be the aggressor.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 288,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 289,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic has no creatures on battlefield but has Ebony Fly available to activate for {4} (exactly the untapped mana available). Coach is at 4hp with no creatures to block. Activating Ebony Fly and rolling a 4+ on d6 would create a flying creature that could attack for lethal. Even a smaller roll deals unblockable damage against an empty board.",
      "action_taken": "Passed on activating Ebony Fly during combat, declining to create a potential attacker against a defenseless opponent at 4 life.",
      "better_line": "Activate Ebony Fly for {4} to roll a d6 and potentially become a flying creature. With Coach at 4 life and no blockers, rolling 4+ wins the game immediately, and any result deals chip damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 311,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 317,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3P Coach has Anger in the graveyard and controls a Swamp (and Akoum Refuge which can produce R/B, plus other lands). However, Anger's ability requires controlling a Mountain, not just any land. Coach has no Mountain on the battlefield (the Mountains are in hand and graveyard). The game engine offered Akroma as an attacker, which means either Akroma somehow doesn't have summoning sickness (perhaps cast on a previous turn or morphed earlier) or there's a rules engine issue. Regardless, Coach declined to attack with a 6/6 flying trampler when both opponents are eliminated (-2hp and -1hp) and only Gem3F Stoic remains at 34 life. With Coach at 15 life and only 2 Mountains in hand with no board presence besides lands and Akroma, attacking with the 6/6 flyer is critical to applying pressure and racing before Stoic rebuilds. Declining the attack wastes a combat step with the most powerful creature on the board.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to attack with Akroma, Angel of Fury, confused about whether it had haste.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Akroma, Angel of Fury for 6 flying/trample damage to Gem3F Stoic (the only remaining opponent), bringing them to 28 life and applying necessary pressure.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 321,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 334,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Stoic skipped their main phase without playing Mishra's Factory (a free land drop that can become a 2/2 attacker) and without casting Diviner's Portent to find threats. With no creatures on board and needing to close out the game against Gem3P Coach at 15 life, they should at minimum make their land drop. Mishra's Factory can attack as a 2/2 and provides colorless mana.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority and moved to combat with no creatures and without playing a land.",
      "better_line": "Play Mishra's Factory, then either activate it and attack for 2, or cast Diviner's Portent for X=4 or 5 to draw cards and find threats to close out the game.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 325,
      "player": "Gem3F Stoic",
      "decision_index": 338,
    }
